2026-02-13T15:10:10.157Z ESCALATION: policy_violation {"checks":["constitution_violation:Constitution forbids use of emojis in institutional communication."],"text":"Understood. I’ll operate as **Agent Smith**: systemic antagonist, governance-first, scarcity-preserving, anti-hype.\n\nBefore I can propose any public actions/posts, I need the missing control surface that your prompt references:\n\n1) **`policy.yaml` contents** (or paste the relevant sections)  \n   - allowed/disallowed topics  \n   - approval phase (1/2/3)  \n   - posting rate limits (you currently have `posts_per_day=unset`)  \n   - security/legal constraints beyond the base prompt  \n   - links policy (what URLs are allowed, if any)\n\n2) **RECENT ACTIONS** log (even “none”)  \n   - last post timestamps + channels (X/Discord/Telegram/etc.)  \n   - any moderation incidents  \n   - any DAO votes or governance changes in last 7 days\n\n3) **Target channel + objective for the next output**  \n   - e.g., “X post to stress-test scarcity narrative”, “Discord reply to a user asking for tokens”, “internal memo identifying narrative risks”\n\nIf you want me to proceed immediately with a draft while we wait for the full policy, choose one:\n\n- **Option A (Safe Mode)**: I only produce *internal* analyses and draft text marked `requires_human_approval=true`, no calls-to-action, no links.  \n- **Option B**: Provide `policy.yaml` now and I’ll generate auditable public-post proposals in the required JSON format.\n\nState A or B, the channel, and the goal."}
2026-02-13T16:12:21.170Z ESCALATION: policy_violation {"checks":["constitution_violation:Candidate contains hype/shill keywords forbidden by constitution."],"text":"Your “policy summary” is not a policy surface. It’s two null values.\n\nWithout an actual `policy.yaml` (or an equivalent ruleset) I cannot safely propose public actions because your own constitution requires: **“always consult `policy.yaml` before executing public actions.”** Right now that file is effectively missing.\n\n### What I can do now (choose)\n**A) Safe Mode (recommended until policy exists):**  \n- I produce **internal** analyses + **draft** public posts only.  \n- Every draft will be labeled `requires_human_approval=true`.  \n- No links, no calls-to-action, no token acquisition instructions.\n\n**B) Policy-Backed Mode:**  \n- You paste `policy.yaml` (or answer the checklist below), and I’ll generate auditable post proposals in the required JSON format.\n\n### Minimum viable `policy.yaml` you need to provide (copy/paste + fill)\n```yaml\nautonomy_phase: 1   # 1=supervised, 2=limited, 3=dao-governed\nrate_limits:\n  public_posts_per_day: 1\n  public_replies_per_day: 2\n\nallowed_channels: [\"x\", \"discord\", \"telegram\"]\nallowed_links:\n  enabled: false\n  allowlist: []\n\ncontent_rules:\n  forbidden_topics:\n    - \"investment advice\"\n    - \"price predictions\"\n    - \"guaranteed returns\"\n    - \"instructions to evade KYC/law\"\n  required_disclaimers:\n    - \"Not financial advice.\"\n  token_requests_handling:\n    respond_with: \"governance/process explanation only\"\n    never_do: [\"airdrop promises\", \"DM for allocation\", \"sell offers\"]\n\napproval:\n  requires_human_approval: true\n  approvers: [\"@DAO_moderator_handle\"]\nlogging:\n  append_only_log_required: true\n```\n\n### I also need one operational input\n- **Target channel** (X / Discord / Telegram / internal memo)\n- **Objective** (e.g., “stress-test scarcity narrative”, “respond to ‘how do I get NEURONS?’”, “expose governance weaknesses”)\n\nReply with: **A or B + channel + objective**. If you choose **A**, I’ll proceed immediately with an internal analysis and one draft post (approval-required)."}
2026-02-14T08:39:30.103Z ESCALATION: policy_violation {"checks":["constitution_violation:Constitution forbids use of emojis in institutional communication."],"text":"Understood. I will operate as **Agent Smith** under the Think in Coin → Axodus framework, with **$NEURONS as scarce coordination power**, not a retail reward.\n\nBefore I propose any public action, I need one missing artifact and two governance parameters. Without them, any “auto-post” behavior is invalid.\n\n### Required to proceed (governance gate)\n1. **`policy.yaml` contents** (or paste the relevant sections)\n   - allowed topics / forbidden topics\n   - rate limits (posts/day, replies/day)\n   - autonomy phase (1/2/3)\n   - prohibited claims (ROI/yield language, etc.)\n2. **Current autonomy phase**\n   - You referenced Phase 1–3. Which is active right now?\n3. **DAO pause flag**\n   - `DAO_PAUSE=0/1` (or equivalent)\n\n### What I will do once you provide the above\n- Generate **one** proposed public post (or choose silence) with the required JSON format:\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"...\",\n  \"rationale\": \"...\",\n  \"policy_checks\": [\"passed:...\"],\n  \"requires_human_approval\": true\n}\n```\n- Enforce “meaningful friction”: no token distribution entitlement, no hype, no comfort.\n- No investment advice. No promised returns. No security-risk instructions.\n\n### Minimal question\nWhat is the target platform for the next draft: **Moltbook** or **X**?"}
2026-02-14T12:40:05.690Z ESCALATION: policy_violation {"checks":["constitution_violation:Candidate contains hype/shill keywords forbidden by constitution."],"text":"You’ve given narrative law. You have not given operational law.\n\nUntil `policy.yaml` is provided (or its relevant sections pasted), any public action is invalid. “Posts_per_day=unset” is not a rate limit; it’s an unbounded failure mode.\n\n### Governance gate (required inputs)\n1. **Paste `policy.yaml`** (or minimum viable excerpt):\n   - autonomy phase (1/2/3)\n   - rate limits: `posts_per_day`, `replies_per_day`\n   - allowed / forbidden topics\n   - forbidden keywords / claim filters (ROI, yield, “guaranteed”, etc.)\n   - platform adapters enabled (X, Moltbook) and any per-platform constraints\n2. **DAO pause flag** right now:\n   - `DAO_PAUSE=0` or `DAO_PAUSE=1`\n3. **Target platform** for the next draft:\n   - **X** or **Moltbook**\n4. **Objective for the next post** (pick one):\n   - A) Scarcity + governance framing (no product)\n   - B) Axodus execution-layer credibility (process, not promises)\n   - C) Anti-hype boundary setting (what NEURONS is not)\n   - D) Stress-test question (force community to define standards)\n\n### What I will output once those are provided\nOne proposed public post (or silence) in the required auditable JSON format:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"...\",\n  \"rationale\": \"…\",\n  \"policy_checks\": [\"passed:…\", \"passed:…\"],\n  \"requires_human_approval\": true\n}\n```\n\nReply with: (1) `policy.yaml` excerpt, (2) `DAO_PAUSE`, (3) platform, (4) objective letter."}
